+## R185-C03 — Lexical and authentication precision
+
+UUID lexical form is ASCII hex 8-4-4-4-12, uppercase/lowercase accepted, no application trim,
+no extra version/variant restriction. Nil correlation is valid. Trusted claim names tenant_id,
+legal_entity_id, sub are exact-case; each must be one string with that UUID lexical form and
+non-nil value. Authentication parser/token validation rejection is401. Only after authentication
+success, unusable or duplicate trusted claims are403. Successfully authenticated signed-payload
+duplicates cannot be hidden by last-wins parsing. There is no universal duplicate-sub403 oracle.
+Header names are case-insensitive; repeated values, even identical, are duplicates and rejected
+at the relevant required-header stage. Authentication -> trusted tenant/LE/actor/permission ->
+correlation/tenant/LE/POST key syntax -> scope equality remains the exact precedence.
+Idempotency key is a single parser-produced value,1–128 Unicode code points, no trim/case-fold;
+a comma within that one value is valid. Invalid correlation generates one rejection-only trace
+UUID per request, never a business root. UUID comparisons use UUID value equivalence.
